Z||000001||william_thorniii||02-01-2000||09:42 PM||||Eddie,<P>Be VERY careful if you relocate the ECM.  It must be well ventilated for longevity.  Remember Pontiac even vented it when it was in the passenger compartment.  I know that ECM relocation is common, but you must make sure that it can breathe... otherwise your engnine won't be running long.  Now to respond to the topic... take your time, I am not in a hurry.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||4
